6) with John taking the bronze in 14:39.8.","id":"B174-14","w":"June 1970"},{"f":"crops/B224/B224-p43-flashback-1970-surrey-xc.jpg","c":"January 3rd 1970 at Milford Heath and no. 80, Bob Holt (Hercules Wimbledon), leads the Surrey Senior Cross Country Championships from no. 13, Gerry North (Belgrave). Bob eventually won with Gerry runner up and Dave Holt, pictured behind Bob, 3rd. Also to be seen are Chris Wade of Ranelagh (brother of tennis star Virginia), no. 11 Adrian Major (Belgrave) who placed 5th, no. 77, Mick Fuller (Hercules Wimbledon) and we can just spot Bob Gevers (SLH). Hercules Wimbledon won the team race from Mitcham with the Bels. 3rd.","id":"B224-118","w":"June 1996"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B161/B161-p43-national-backpiece-montage.jpg","caption":"BACKPIECE PHOTOS: TOP LEFT: Barefooted Hart in the throes of a 9 miles battle with Dai Davies (TVH) who pipped him by one place. TOP RIGHT: Bicourt leads Ward (Man.DLC), Billings (Sutt.in A) and team-mate O'Hara. John finished one place ahead of Billings and 23 up on Ward. BOTTOM: A desperate North fights to hold off Bob Holt, Peter Welsh (Empire S'chase gold-medallist) and Mike Turner.","source":"B161-66","when":"March 1967"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Bob Holt in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1964–1997: 102 mentions in 36 issues, 58 race results and 6 photographs.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B162/B162-p35-holt-thresher-surrey-3-miles.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-bob-holt.html"},"legend":false}